$DIR/test.p:3:7: the last result of one() has type int, not error; or tests a last result of type error
    The call before or must return a result of type error last, and the type
    must be error itself. A function that returns no error, or no result at all,
    cannot fail in a way that or can see. A type that implements error, a
    defined type based on error, or a type parameter is not accepted either.
    Remove the or clause, or change the function so that its last result has
    type error.
    With the type exactly error, the test is always the nil test of one
    interface type, and err in the clause is the result itself, not a conversion
    of it.
    Return the error as an error:
        func parse(s string) (int, error)
    (see "Or clauses" in the Plutonium spec, section 11.27)
    (run "pluto explain E2462" for a longer explanation)

